    "how": {"x": 0, "y": -170, "w": 1280, "size": "m", "fill": "blue", "text": "Press Play on an option. The bar on top of each switches screens (Idle, Recording, Processing, Report, Settings, First run) and Light/Dark. Inside the Mac screen, the buttons work too: Record, Pause, Stop, open a report. Invented data only."},
    "hig": {"x": 1360, "y": -170, "w": 1280, "size": "m", "fill": "orange", "text": "Apple HIG, read 2026-11-07: Liquid Glass only on controls and navigation (sidebar, toolbar, menus, pill), never on the report or lists. One prominent action, on the trailing side. A menu bar extra opens a menu, not a popover, and the user turns it on. Determinate progress with Pause and Cancel for downloads. Custom screen before the system permission prompt."},
